# Docker reads .dockerignore from the root of the *build context*, which for
# this image is apps/api — the repository-root .dockerignore does not apply.
#
# Patterns are NOT .gitignore syntax: a trailing slash does not mean "this
# directory at any depth". Use **/ explicitly, or nested caches slip into the
# image (verified — host .pyc files were being baked in).

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/.env
**/.env.local

# tests/ is deliberately NOT excluded. The dev stage exists to run them, and CI
# runs pytest inside that image with no bind mount to fall back on — excluding
# them here means pytest collects nothing and exits 5. Shipping a few KB of
# tests in the runtime image is the cheaper trade.
